# sed -f script for `make anon_zip` to scrub author identity from the
# submission tarball. Copy this file to `.anon_patterns` (gitignored) and
# fill in your own identity tokens, then `make anon_zip`.
#
# Each line is a sed command. Use `s|pat|repl|g` (pipe delimiter so URLs
# don't need escaping). Order: most-specific first.
#
# Example:
#   s|https://github.com/<your-username>/decept-bench|<repo-URL-withheld-for-double-blind-review>|g
#   s|<your-username>|anonymous|g
#   s|<Your Full Name>|Anonymous Authors|g
#   s|"<YourFamilyName>"|"Anonymous"|g
#   s|"<YourGivenName>"|""|g
#   s|<your-email>@<domain>|anonymous@example.invalid|g
#
# After `make anon_zip`, manually grep the staged tree at
# /tmp/decept-bench-anon for any tokens you missed before uploading
# submission.zip.

s|https://github.com/<your-username>/decept-bench|<repo-URL-withheld-for-double-blind-review>|g
s|github.com/<your-username>/decept-bench|<repo-URL-withheld-for-double-blind-review>|g
